Embedded React: move a translated node's subtree with it.

Modified from Embedded React (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Cory Lamming) at the
revision pinned in dependencies.lock.json, after the patches listed before this
one there. Changed files: engine/scene/compositor.c,
engine/tests/rendering/CMakeLists.txt and the new
engine/tests/rendering/test_anim_translate_offscreen.c. Proposed upstream as
pull request #311.

The translate-only fast path offset a node's own paint by its translate but
handed its children the untranslated offset, so they kept painting at their
layout boxes. A header slid up past the screen's top edge left its items
behind, frozen on screen. The fast path now passes the translate down with the
scroll offset, and the damage passes measure descendants the same way
(node_ancestor_scroll), so the trail they vacate is repainted. Translates that
go through the transform capture already moved their subtree and are unchanged.

